  "notes": [
    "Each part file holds one node at its own origin; that origin is the pivot. Place the file under a node at `pivot` and move or turn that node as the part says.",
    "screen.glb's UVs map the disc inscribed in the unit square: texture (0.5, 0.5) at the centre, the image's top edge at 12 o'clock (glTF V down). An app can instead draw its own disc from `screen`.",
    "link.glb is one strap link with its hinge at the origin, reaching along +Y. A strap is a chain: link 0 at the strap's anchor, each next link at (0, pitch, 0) in the one before, each turned about its own X by rest_deg + flex * flex_deg. The bottom strap's anchor is turned 180 degrees about Z, so the same angles curl it back too.",
    "The light strips are not in the part files, so the app can draw, tint and pulse them. They are in watch.glb only, with emissive materials that use KHR_materials_emissive_strength."
  ],
